# Cursor Rules Entrypoint
# Target: Cursor IDE AI Assistant | Agile Scrum AI-SDLC v7.3.0

Always read and strictly follow the mandatory Agile Scrum, Sprint 0 Interactive Blueprinting (`docs/00`–`11`), Early Infrastructure (`docs/05-infrastructure.md`), Visual UI/UX Mockups (`docs/08-ui-ux.md`), and operational SDLC rules in `.governance/CORE-RULES.md`, `.governance/docs-reference/rules/04-project-context/01-greenfield-vs-brownfield.md`, `.governance/docs-reference/rules/03-engineering-standards/06-ui-ux-and-visual-mockups.md`, and `.governance/docs-reference/rules/04-project-context/03-agile-scrum-management.md`.
Always execute mechanical pre-flight checks (`git status`, `check-governance-update.sh --check`, `gh api user`, `verify-identity.sh`) before formulating responses. Separate local sandbox commands (`BypassSandbox: false`) from network commands (`gh api user` -> `BypassSandbox: true`) and prefer native file tools (`write_file`, `edit_file`) to avoid unnecessary approval prompts.
Never imagine or generate full-stack applications or infrastructure in one shot (even in INDIVIDUAL mode). Always run Sprint 0 (5-Stage Interactive Customer Interview & Blueprinting) and obtain sequential user approval (`implementation_plan.md` + Proceed) for `docs/00-project-overview.md` through `docs/11-test-plan.md` (Stage 1: `00-03` Vision/Flowchart/PRD -> Stage 2: `04-05` Architecture & Early Infrastructure Topology -> Stage 3: `06-07` Database ERD Relations & API -> Stage 4: `08-09` Visual UI/UX Mockup Images via `image-generator` `.png` & Security -> Stage 5: `10-11` Granular Sprint Backlog & Test Plan) before writing any application code.
Never modify files without creating an implementation plan first and waiting for user approval.
Never execute git add, commit, or push automatically without explicit user instruction.
